---
import "../styles/global.css";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";



const me = {
  icon: "✨",
  title: "That's Me — Mariana",
  keywords: "ENGINEER · MAKER · CURIOUS · ALWAYS BUILDING SOMETHING",
  description:
    "I'm curious by nature and I like having many sides to explore. I enjoy making things with my hands, challenging myself physically, getting lost in a good story, learning something new, and spending time with the animals I love. I'm also someone who enjoys being out and about, making plans that are a little out of the ordinary, and saying yes when an opportunity to experience something new comes along I guess I like to live up to my last name. Whether it's taking a long walk, trying a new activity, going somewhere I've never been, or finding a challenge that puts my mind to work, I'd rather experience something than wonder what it would have been like. I can enjoy both adventure and quiet moments, but what connects them all is my curiosity and my willingness to try. I don't think I have just one way of being, and I like the fact that there is always something new to discover.",
};

const hobbies = [
  {
    position: "top",
    icon: "🏃",
    title: "Sports & Movement",
    keywords: "RUNNING · SKATING · DANCING · HIKING · BRAZILIAN JIU-JITSU · MUAY THAI",
    description:
      "Movement has found its way into my life for different reasons, and each one has taught me something along the way. Mixed martial arts taught me humility from the very beginning: there will always be someone stronger or more skilled than you, and not everyone is willing to meet you at your level. You learn to respect others, accept what you don't know, and keep showing up willing to learn. Running started for a different reason: I wanted to give my dog a healthier lifestyle, and somehow, that goal became part of my own routine too. Skating, on the other hand, has been with me since childhood. I used to train and even compete in races, but today I enjoy it in a different way, going skating with my school friends and keeping a little piece of that childhood passion alive. And then there's dancing. To me, there are few better ways to be fully present, to stop overthinking and simply experience the moment. I honestly think everyone should dance, not because they have to be good at it, but because sometimes the best thing you can do is let go, listen to the music, and enjoy being there.",
  },
  {
    position: "right",
    icon: "🎨",
    title: "Art & Expression",
    keywords:
      "MUSIC · STOP-MOTION · HANDMADE · EXPERIMENTATION · CRAFT · CREATIVITY",
    description:
      "I've always been drawn to making things, whether it's bringing a melody to life, building something from scratch, or experimenting with a material I've never worked with before. Music is one of the ways I express myself: I enjoy playing the ukulele and harmonica, and I love how a few notes can change the mood of a moment. I'm also fascinated by stop-motion animation and the magic of making something inanimate feel alive, one frame at a time. That fascination has grown to the point where I'm designing my own armature, exploring what goes on behind the scenes to bring a character to life. I love that this kind of creativity combines imagination with patience, mechanics, and a little bit of magic. That same curiosity follows me into the things I make by hand. I've explored everything from crochet, embroidery, and sewing my own clothes to ceramics, stained glass, jewellery, linocut printing, and mobiles. I'm always tempted to try a new technique, discover what a material can do, or find a way to turn an idea in my head into something tangible. For me, creating isn't about sticking to one medium or mastering just one craft; it's about experimenting, learning as I go, and enjoying the satisfaction of making something that didn't exist before.",
  },
  {
    position: "bottom",
    icon: "♟️",
    title: "Mind & Strategy",
    keywords: "READING · SCIENCE · FANTASY · CHESS · JIGSAW PUZZLES · CURIOSITY",
    description:
      "I'm always looking for something interesting to discover, whether it's through a scientific article or a fantasy novel. I love reading because it lets me do two things I enjoy equally: learn about the world around me and escape into completely different ones. Sometimes I read to stay informed, explore an idea, or understand something new; other times, I just want to get lost in a story and switch off for a while. Either way, there's always something that keeps me turning the pages. Chess gives my curiosity a different kind of challenge. I enjoy thinking ahead, recognizing patterns, and figuring out how one move can change the whole game. And then there are jigsaw puzzles, which have become a little personal challenge of their own. When I'm alone, I've developed a habit of trying to complete them in record time, almost turning them into a race against myself. When I'm doing one with other people, though, I take my time and enjoy the process together. I like that the same activity can become either a challenge or a way to slow down, depending on how I choose to experience it.",
  },
  {
    position: "left",
    icon: "🐾",
    title: "Animals & Companionship",
    keywords:
      "FRIDA · DALI · MATISSE · PERSONALITIES · EMPATHY · COMPANIONSHIP",
    description:
      "My pets are a huge part of my life, and each of them has a little story of their own. Frida, my dog, came into my life when I adopted her at just three months old during a trip to Urrao, a town in Antioquia. She's always been a little like a cat herself: independent, exceptionally well-behaved, and perfectly happy doing her own thing. Over time, though, I started feeling that she was getting a little bored, and that changed when Dali and Matisse joined our family two years later, also at three months old. They are brother and sister from the same litter, born to a cat belonging to a friend I've known since school. They were the only two kittens in the litter, and they couldn't be more different from Frida. In many ways, they're more like dogs: they greet people who come into our home and want to be part of absolutely everything that's going on. Perhaps that's why the three of them get along so well. They each have their own personality, but somehow, they've found their own way of being together, playing, and keeping one another company. Living with them has taught me more than I ever expected. They've helped me learn to manage stress, practice patience, and approach situations with greater empathy. Caring for three different personalities has taught me to look beyond the obvious, consider different needs, and think about how to prevent problems rather than simply react to them. I've come to appreciate how creating a kinder, more balanced environment starts with understanding those around you. Above all, they bring me joy, make ordinary days feel special, and remind me how much we can learn from the bonds we build with other living beings.",
  },
];

---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />

    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"
    />

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Hobbies and interests of Mariana Calle Méndez, beyond engineering."
    />

    <title>Hobbies — Mariana Calle</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <Navbar />

    <main class="experience-bg">

      <div class="experience-shell">

        <!-- =====================================================
             HEADER
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="experience-header">
          <p class="section-label">
            BEYOND ENGINEERING
          </p>

          <h1>HOBBIES</h1>

          <p class="experience-intro">
            The things that inspire me, move me, and keep me creative.
          </p>
        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             HOBBY ORBIT
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="experience-timeline hobbies-main">

          <div class="experience-card hobby-card">

            <div class="hobby-orbit">

              <!-- Decorative connection lines -->
              <div class="orbit-line line-top"></div>
              <div class="orbit-line line-right"></div>
              <div class="orbit-line line-bottom"></div>
              <div class="orbit-line line-left"></div>


              <!-- =================================================
                   TOP — SPORTS
              ================================================== -->

              {
                hobbies.map((hobby, index) => (
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class={`orbit-chip orbit-${hobby.position}`}
                    data-index={index}
                    aria-pressed="false"
                  >
                    <span
                      class="orbit-icon"
                      aria-hidden="true"
                    >
                      {hobby.icon}
                    </span>

                    <span class="orbit-title">
                      {hobby.title}
                    </span>

                    <span class="orbit-keywords">
                      {hobby.keywords}
                    </span>
                  </button>
                ))
              }


              <!-- =================================================
                   CENTER — YOU
              ================================================== -->

              <button
                type="button"
                class="orbit-avatar active"
                id="orbit-avatar"
                aria-pressed="true"
                aria-label="About me"
              >
                <img
                  src="/hobbies/yo.png"
                  alt="Sticker illustration of Mariana wearing a red bucket hat and goggles"
                />

                <span class="avatar-label">
                  THAT'S ME
                </span>
              </button>

            </div>


            <!-- =================================================
                 SELECTED HOBBY
                 (por defecto muestra "That's Me")
            ================================================== -->

            <div class="hobby-detail" aria-live="polite">

              <div class="detail-heading">

                <span
                  class="detail-icon"
                  id="detail-icon"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  {me.icon}
                </span>

                <div>
                  <p class="detail-label" id="detail-label">
                    ABOUT
                  </p>

                  <h2 id="detail-title">
                    {me.title}
                  </h2>
                </div>

              </div>


              <div class="detail-divider"></div>


              <p
                class="detail-description"
                id="detail-description"
              >
                {me.description}
              </p>


              <div class="detail-keywords" id="detail-keywords">
                {me.keywords}
              </div>

            </div>

          </div>

        </section>

      </div>

    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>


<script>
  const me = {
    icon: "✨",
    title: "That's Me — Mariana",
    label: "ABOUT",
    keywords: "ENGINEER · MAKER · CURIOUS · ALWAYS BUILDING SOMETHING",
    description:
      "I'm curious by nature and I like having many sides to explore. I enjoy making things with my hands, challenging myself physically, getting lost in a good story, learning something new, and spending time with the animals I love. I'm also someone who enjoys being out and about, making plans that are a little out of the ordinary, and saying yes when an opportunity to experience something new comes along I guess I like to live up to my last name. Whether it's taking a long walk, trying a new activity, going somewhere I've never been, or finding a challenge that puts my mind to work, I'd rather experience something than wonder what it would have been like. I can enjoy both adventure and quiet moments, but what connects them all is my curiosity and my willingness to try. I don't think I have just one way of being, and I like the fact that there is always something new to discover.",
  };

  const hobbies = [
    {
      icon: "🏃",
      title: "Sports & Movement",
      label: "CURRENTLY EXPLORING",
      keywords:
        "RUNNING · SKATING · DANCING · HIKING · BRAZILIAN JIU-JITSU · MUAY THAI",
      description:
        "Movement has found its way into my life for different reasons, and each one has taught me something along the way. Mixed martial arts taught me humility from the very beginning: there will always be someone stronger or more skilled than you, and not everyone is willing to meet you at your level. You learn to respect others, accept what you don't know, and keep showing up willing to learn. Running started for a different reason: I wanted to give my dog a healthier lifestyle, and somehow, that goal became part of my own routine too. Skating, on the other hand, has been with me since childhood. I used to train and even compete in races, but today I enjoy it in a different way, going skating with my school friends and keeping a little piece of that childhood passion alive. And then there's dancing. To me, there are few better ways to be fully present, to stop overthinking and simply experience the moment. I honestly think everyone should dance, not because they have to be good at it, but because sometimes the best thing you can do is let go, listen to the music, and enjoy being there.",
    },
    {
      icon: "🎨",
      title: "Art & Expression",
      label: "CURRENTLY EXPLORING",
      keywords:
        "MUSIC · STOP-MOTION · HANDMADE · EXPERIMENTATION · CRAFT · CREATIVITY",
      description:
        "I've always been drawn to making things, whether it's bringing a melody to life, building something from scratch, or experimenting with a material I've never worked with before. Music is one of the ways I express myself: I enjoy playing the ukulele and harmonica, and I love how a few notes can change the mood of a moment. I'm also fascinated by stop-motion animation and the magic of making something inanimate feel alive, one frame at a time. That fascination has grown to the point where I'm designing my own armature, exploring what goes on behind the scenes to bring a character to life. I love that this kind of creativity combines imagination with patience, mechanics, and a little bit of magic. That same curiosity follows me into the things I make by hand. I've explored everything from crochet, embroidery, and sewing my own clothes to ceramics, stained glass, jewellery, linocut printing, and mobiles. I'm always tempted to try a new technique, discover what a material can do, or find a way to turn an idea in my head into something tangible. For me, creating isn't about sticking to one medium or mastering just one craft; it's about experimenting, learning as I go, and enjoying the satisfaction of making something that didn't exist before.",
    },
    {
      icon: "♟️",
      title: "Mind & Strategy",
      label: "CURRENTLY EXPLORING",
      keywords:
        "READING · SCIENCE · FANTASY · CHESS · JIGSAW PUZZLES · CURIOSITY",
      description:
        "I'm always looking for something interesting to discover, whether it's through a scientific article or a fantasy novel. I love reading because it lets me do two things I enjoy equally: learn about the world around me and escape into completely different ones. Sometimes I read to stay informed, explore an idea, or understand something new; other times, I just want to get lost in a story and switch off for a while. Either way, there's always something that keeps me turning the pages. Chess gives my curiosity a different kind of challenge. I enjoy thinking ahead, recognizing patterns, and figuring out how one move can change the whole game. And then there are jigsaw puzzles, which have become a little personal challenge of their own. When I'm alone, I've developed a habit of trying to complete them in record time, almost turning them into a race against myself. When I'm doing one with other people, though, I take my time and enjoy the process together. I like that the same activity can become either a challenge or a way to slow down, depending on how I choose to experience it.",
    },
    {
      icon: "🐾",
      title: "Animals & Companionship",
      label: "CURRENTLY EXPLORING",
      keywords:
        "FRIDA · DALI · MATISSE · PERSONALITIES · EMPATHY · COMPANIONSHIP",
      description:
        "My pets are a huge part of my life, and each of them has a little story of their own. Frida, my dog, came into my life when I adopted her at just three months old during a trip to Urrao, a town in Antioquia. She's always been a little like a cat herself: independent, exceptionally well-behaved, and perfectly happy doing her own thing. Over time, though, I started feeling that she was getting a little bored, and that changed when Dali and Matisse joined our family two years later, also at three months old. They are brother and sister from the same litter, born to a cat belonging to a friend I've known since school. They were the only two kittens in the litter, and they couldn't be more different from Frida. In many ways, they're more like dogs: they greet people who come into our home and want to be part of absolutely everything that's going on. Perhaps that's why the three of them get along so well. They each have their own personality, but somehow, they've found their own way of being together, playing, and keeping one another company. Living with them has taught me more than I ever expected. They've helped me learn to manage stress, practice patience, and approach situations with greater empathy. Caring for three different personalities has taught me to look beyond the obvious, consider different needs, and think about how to prevent problems rather than simply react to them. I've come to appreciate how creating a kinder, more balanced environment starts with understanding those around you. Above all, they bring me joy, make ordinary days feel special, and remind me how much we can learn from the bonds we build with other living beings.",
    },
  ];

  const chips =
    Array.from(
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".orbit-chip")
    );

  const avatarButton =
    document.getElementById(
      "orbit-avatar"
    ) as HTMLButtonElement | null;

  const detailIcon =
    document.getElementById("detail-icon");

  const detailLabel =
    document.getElementById("detail-label");

  const detailTitle =
    document.getElementById("detail-title");

  const detailDescription =
    document.getElementById("detail-description");

  const detailKeywords =
    document.getElementById("detail-keywords");

  const detail =
    document.querySelector(".hobby-detail");

  // Por defecto arrancamos mostrando "That's Me", no un hobby.
  let activeIndex: number | "me" = "me";


  function renderDetail(
    source: {
      icon: string;
      title: string;
      label: string;
      description: string;
      keywords: string;
    }
  ) {

    if (detailIcon) {
      detailIcon.textContent = source.icon;
    }

    if (detailLabel) {
      detailLabel.textContent = source.label;
    }

    if (detailTitle) {
      detailTitle.textContent = source.title;
    }

    if (detailDescription) {
      detailDescription.textContent = source.description;
    }

    if (detailKeywords) {
      detailKeywords.textContent = source.keywords;
    }

    detail?.classList.remove("changing");

    requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      detail?.classList.add("changing");

      window.setTimeout(() => {
        detail?.classList.remove("changing");
      }, 350);
    });
  }


  function setActiveChip(index: number | "me") {

    activeIndex = index;

    chips.forEach((chip, chipIndex) => {
      const isActive = chipIndex === index;

      chip.classList.toggle("active", isActive);
      chip.setAttribute(
        "aria-pressed",
        isActive ? "true" : "false"
      );
    });

    avatarButton?.classList.toggle(
      "active",
      index === "me"
    );

    avatarButton?.setAttribute(
      "aria-pressed",
      index === "me" ? "true" : "false"
    );
  }


  function selectHobby(index: number) {
    const hobby = hobbies[index];

    if (!hobby) return;

    setActiveChip(index);
    renderDetail(hobby);
  }


  function selectMe() {
    setActiveChip("me");
    renderDetail(me);
  }


  chips.forEach((chip, index) => {
    chip.addEventListener("click", () => {
      selectHobby(index);
    });
  });


  avatarButton?.addEventListener("click", () => {
    selectMe();
  });


  document.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
    if (
      event.key !== "ArrowRight" &&
      event.key !== "ArrowLeft"
    ) {
      return;
    }

    // Las flechas solo recorren los hobbies; el avatar se
    // selecciona con click/Enter directamente sobre él.
    const currentIndex =
      typeof activeIndex === "number" ? activeIndex : 0;

    const nextIndex =
      event.key === "ArrowRight"
        ? (currentIndex + 1) % hobbies.length
        : (currentIndex - 1 + hobbies.length) % hobbies.length;

    selectHobby(nextIndex);
    chips[nextIndex]?.focus();
  });
</script>


<style>

/* =========================================================
   PAGE STRUCTURE

   Same outer dimensions and visual language as Experience.
   ========================================================= */

.experience-bg {
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 100vh;

  margin: 0;
  padding: 3rem 0 5rem;

  background-image: url("/textures/paper-texture.png");
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center;
  background-attachment: fixed;
  background-color: transparent;

  box-sizing: border-box;
  overflow-x: hidden;
}


.experience-shell {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 1200px;

  margin: 1rem auto 0;
  padding: 2rem;

  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
  border-radius: 16px;

  box-shadow: 0 4px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);

  backdrop-filter: blur(4px);

  box-sizing: border-box;
}


/* =========================================================
   HEADER

   Same dimensions as Experience.
   ========================================================= */

.experience-shell .experience-header {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 950px;

  margin: 0 auto 2rem;
  padding: 3rem 2.5rem;

  text-align: center;

  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
  border-radius: 12px;

  box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);

  box-sizing: border-box;
  overflow: hidden;
}


.section-label {
  margin: 0 0 0.8rem;

  color: var(--color-accent);

  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
}


.experience-header h1 {
  margin: 0;

  color: var(--color-deep);

  font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 6.5vw, 4.6rem);
  line-height: 1.05;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;

  overflow-wrap: break-word;
}


.experience-intro {
  width: min(700px, 100%);

  margin: 1.5rem auto 0;

  color: var(--color-text);

  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.6;

  text-align: center;
}


/* =========================================================
   MAIN HOBBY SECTION

   Same outer dimensions as Experience's timeline card.
   ========================================================= */

.experience-shell .experience-timeline {
  width: 100%;

  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 3rem 2rem 3rem;

  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
  border-radius: 12px;

  box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);

  box-sizing: border-box;
  overflow: hidden;
}


.experience-card {
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
  max-width: 100%;

  box-sizing: border-box;
  overflow: visible;

  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  border-radius: 12px;

  padding: 2.5rem;

  box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);

  backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
}


/* =========================================================
   HOBBY ORBIT
   ========================================================= */

.hobby-orbit {
  position: relative;

  display: grid;

  grid-template-columns:
    minmax(150px, 1fr)
    minmax(180px, 240px)
    minmax(150px, 1fr);

  grid-template-rows:
    minmax(130px, auto)
    minmax(190px, 240px)
    minmax(130px, auto);

  grid-template-areas:
    ". top ."
    "left avatar right"
    ". bottom .";

  align-items: center;
  justify-items: center;

  column-gap: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  row-gap: 1rem;

  min-height: 520px;
}


/* =========================================================
   AVATAR
   ========================================================= */

.orbit-avatar {
  grid-area: avatar;

  position: relative;
  z-index: 5;

  width: clamp(150px, 18vw, 220px);

  background: transparent;

  border: none;

  padding: 0;

  appearance: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  font: inherit;

  filter:
    drop-shadow(0 10px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12));

  animation: avatar-float 4s ease-in-out infinite;

  transition: transform 0.3s ease, filter 0.3s ease;
}


.orbit-avatar:hover {
  transform: translateY(-3px);
}


.orbit-avatar.active {
  filter:
    drop-shadow(0 10px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12))
    drop-shadow(0 0 0 3px var(--color-accent));
}


.orbit-avatar img {
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;

  display: block;

  transform: rotate(-3deg);
}


.avatar-label {
  position: absolute;

  bottom: -1.2rem;
  left: 50%;

  transform: translateX(-50%) rotate(-2deg);

  padding: 0.3rem 0.7rem;

  background: var(--color-accent);
  color: var(--color-bg);

  border-radius: 4px;

  font-family: var(--font-title);
  font-size: 0.55rem;

  letter-spacing: 0.12em;

  white-space: nowrap;

  box-shadow: 2px 3px 0 rgba(75, 46, 31, 0.18);

  transition: transform 0.3s ease;
}


.orbit-avatar.active .avatar-label {
  transform: translateX(-50%) rotate(-2deg) scale(1.06);
}


@keyframes avatar-float {
  0%,
  100% {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  50% {
    transform: translateY(-5px);
  }
}


/* =========================================================
   HOBBY BUTTONS
   ========================================================= */

.orbit-chip {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 4;

  display: flex;

  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;

  width: min(100%, 210px);
  min-height: 110px;

  padding: 1rem;

  text-align: center;

  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);

  border: 1px solid rgba(75, 46, 31, 0.14);
  border-radius: 12px;

  box-shadow:
    0 5px 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07);

  cursor: pointer;

  font-family: var(--font-body);

  transition:
    transform 0.3s ease,
    box-shadow 0.3s ease,
    background 0.3s ease,
    color 0.3s ease,
    opacity 0.3s ease;

  appearance: none;
}


.orbit-chip:hover {
  transform: translateY(-5px) rotate(-1deg);

  box-shadow:
    0 10px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
}


.orbit-chip.active {
  background: var(--color-accent);

  color: var(--color-bg);

  border-color: var(--color-accent);

  transform: translateY(-5px) rotate(-1deg);

  box-shadow:
    5px 7px 0 rgba(75, 46, 31, 0.16);
}


.orbit-icon {
  display: block;

  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;

  font-size: 1.6rem;

  line-height: 1;
}


.orbit-title {
  color: var(--color-deep);

  font-family: var(--font-title);

  font-size: 0.85rem;

  line-height: 1.25;

  text-transform: uppercase;

  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}


.orbit-chip.active .orbit-title {
  color: var(--color-bg);
}


.orbit-keywords {
  display: block;

  margin-top: 0.45rem;

  color: var(--color-text);

  font-size: 0.58rem;

  font-weight: 700;

  line-height: 1.45;

  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}


.orbit-chip.active .orbit-keywords {
  color: var(--color-bg);
  opacity: 0.9;
}


/* =========================================================
   ORBIT POSITIONS
   ========================================================= */

.orbit-top {
  grid-area: top;
}


.orbit-right {
  grid-area: right;
}


.orbit-bottom {
  grid-area: bottom;
}


.orbit-left {
  grid-area: left;
